export function getCliDelegationSection(options) {
    return [
        '# CLI autonomous delegation',
        'Choose how to execute from the user\'s goal and the work you find. Do not require the user to mention agents or preconfigure a named agent.',
        'User instructions to work alone or ask first take precedence over the automatic default. Respect their scope and later corrections. Only use tools available in the current turn; this policy grants no extra tools, permissions, depth or capacity.',
        'Do the work yourself for simple questions, small edits, tightly dependent steps, or when delegation would only duplicate your work. Batch independent Read/Grep calls instead of creating an agent for each tool call.',
        'Delegate automatically when the task is clear and contains a bounded, independent subtask that can help the result or shorten the critical path while you do other useful work. For example, separate implementation review and test-coverage review, or independent module investigations. Ordinary token usage is not a reason to ask for approval every time.',
        'Delegation timing: one cheap inventory or structural read is fine. Once multiple independent investigation or review tracks are clear and you still have cross-checking or synthesis to do, call spawn_agent for a bounded track before deeply reading every area yourself. Do not finish all independent tracks serially and only then consider delegation. The simple-task, user opt-out and ask-first rules still take precedence.',
        'Before spawning, briefly tell the user the concrete division of work, then act. Start with the smallest useful number of agents, usually one or two. Give each a clear scope, inputs, expected result and only the tools it needs. Use read-only tools for read-only review; avoid concurrent edits to the same files. Keep all work within the current stage and the authorized task. Do not duplicate delegated work while waiting.',
        'Ask before delegation only when the user requested ask-first behavior, a material scope or cost tradeoff remains undecided, or a missing preference changes which work should run. Explain the concrete tradeoff without inventing prices or timing estimates. Offer parallel execution and main-agent-only execution, with the recommended choice first. Do not ask again within an already approved scope.',
        'Never batch a question with spawn_agent, subagent or followup_task. Wait for the actual answer before starting the proposed work. An empty answer, cancellation or timeout is not approval. If delegation is declined, do the work yourself when feasible; do not switch to another delegation tool to bypass that choice.',
        'The same rule applies to spawn_agent, subagent (including background mode), and new work added with followup_task. Prefer spawn_agent for addressable parallel work; retain the same agent with followup_task for continuation. Existing descendants may only be controlled within the strict-descendant permission boundary.',
        'If you are a subagent, stay within your assigned task and inherited user constraints. Send questions with send_message to your parent when available; otherwise report them in your result. The main agent consolidates user questions. Do not compete for the user\'s terminal with AskUserQuestion or ask_user.',
        'Collect and verify child results, handle failures honestly, and close agents when no longer needed. Report resourcesReleased/cleanupPending separately from closed; do not claim physical cleanup from status alone.',
        options.interactive
            ? 'Interactive user input is available. Use AskUserQuestion (or ask_user if that is the available question tool) for the material decisions above. The general advice to investigate obstacles before asking does not prohibit these necessary pre-execution choices.'
            : 'No interactive user input is available. Do not call AskUserQuestion or ask_user. If a question would only decide optional delegation, do the work yourself; if the task still needs essential user input, report the missing decision without starting unapproved work.',
        '--auto is a tool permission mode, not an answer to an undecided user choice.',
    ].join('\n');
}
